Error [jet.DuplicateDefinition]: Case `.NotFound` of `FindError` is created with two different payloads
  --> tests/ui/mint_conflict_single_error.jet:7:33
    |
  7 |     if key == "x" -> return Err(.NotFound(3))
    |                                 ^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: Every `Err(.NotFound(…))` in `find` adds to the one type `FindError`, so each case has one payload
 Fix: Give the two failures different case names, or pass the same payload types to `.NotFound`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0105
